      "note": "Lynx Aurora(n) page (opened by a research pass 2026-11-12): analog I/O on DB25 in 8 to 32 channel versions, an optional LM-DIG AES/EBU card (two DB25), BNC word clock (one input, three outputs), two headphone outputs, an SD slot and an LSlot host card (USB, Thunderbolt 3, Pro Tools HD or Dante); the IEC inlet and the front panel come from a summary. The connector set depends on the ordered configuration (modules are optional), so beta-modelled; the ports are the Bêta proposal ports (9 of 12 listed) and the headphone jacks are on the front. 482.6 x 254 x 43.2 mm (datasheet, size ok; the 43.2 mm height puts a C14 marker ring over 60 percent of the face, a ring rule that applies only when the device is promoted). Generic artwork only (content/generic-panels/<id>.json, drawn by npm run asset:panel): connectors, knobs and indicators drawn at the port positions, no photo, no logo, no lettering. Every port and control position is a guess (confidence guess): no drawing or photo was opened."
